{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 105, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the direct input-to-output residual path helps most when no 0->3 path exists at all, as in experiments 3-4 with gains up to +16 on IN16."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the residual skip with a conv removes the identity path and hurts (experiment 13), while filling an empty edge 3 helps (experiment 14)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the input-output skip destroys the residual shortcut, which is the most damaging deletion in this space."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, edge 5 carries most of the deep feature flow into the output, so swapping its conv for pooling hurts much more (experiments 15 vs 16)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op on the final edge with parameter-free pooling removes key learned capacity, which hurts more than replacing weaker ops."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading pooling to conv on the final edge gives a large gain (experiments 1-2), whereas the same edit applied to stronger ops gains little or nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Deeper conv capacity on edge 5 is easier to exploit when a residual shortcut stabilizes training (experiment 1 vs 2)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Converting a pooling edge into the output to a 3x3 conv adds learnable capacity, unlike edits applied to edges that already hold convs."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "An extra skip on edge 4 is redundant when the input-output residual already exists and only displaces a conv (experiments 19 vs 20)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 missing, node 1 feeds fewer downstream paths, so changing edge 0 matters less (experiments 17 vs 18)."}], "tok": 14599, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "